WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.500
Actually.

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.700
Robert's wife told me.

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:04.760
I've been talking with her a lot, comforting her.

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:07.660
We asked her not to share that info, she promised us she didn't.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:08.700
Well, she's been distraught.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:09.920
She might not I remember.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:10.680
Uh huh.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:11.160
Flimsy.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.700
So what did you mean when you said that you hadn't been to Vernon in 20 years?

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:15.860
My uncle has a cabin there.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:17.100
I would visit him as a kid.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:17.460
Wow.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.960
So your uncle owns a cabin in the town that the body was found.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:22.220
That is quite a coincidence.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.780
I haven't been there for 20 years.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.200
You can call my uncle if you want.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:25.920
Oh, we are.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.140
So you might as well just confess now, or we can take our sweet time like.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.780
the mer jestic slow th.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.500
Either way, we've got you.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:35.200
We don't have him.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:36.760
But I just told him we did have him.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.320
Philip's uncle said he hasn't been to the cabin in months and spoken to

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:40.130
Philip in over a year.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:40.900
what about the neighbors?

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.020
There's only one other house that road and we haven't been able to contact the owner.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:45.320
Yeah, but Philip doesn't know that.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.390
He's rattled right now.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.440
If We tell him the neighbor saw him that night, he'll crack for sure.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:49.200
So you want us to lie?

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.360
No, I want me to lie and for you to stand behind me and say,

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:54.960
like, three oh damn s when I really get cooking.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:56.300
All right, fine, two oh damns.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:57.140
One oh damn?

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.700
There will be no oh damns.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:00.860
But it will be so satisfying in your deep, powerful voice.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:01.580
We're not lying.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:02.300
It's legal.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.520
The Supreme Court said that we're allowed to lie in an interrogation.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.840
I told a perp that I knew Steph Curry a couple of days ago.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.640
It had nothing to do with the case, but I could say it.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:09.560
It's a tactical mistake.

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.150
You're guessing what happened that night.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.600
But what if Philip never went to the cabin?

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:13.240
He did.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.740
I can feel it here.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:15.280
Your stomach?

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:16.080
No, my gut.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.780
Your gut, or intestines, is lower.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.660
You should point down here, closer to your pubis.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:20.160
I'm good.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:21.120
Suppose you're wrong.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:22.840
Now Philip knows we have nothing.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:24.980
There goes our credibility and our leverage.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:27.960
No, we need a different strategy, All right, fine.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.120
How about this.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.180
I convince him I'm unstable.
